    "specPath": "specs/207-the-registry-lists-what-verify-would-run/spec.md",
    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "`registry list` filters by lifecycle status only. Adopters that run every implemented spec's acceptance keep that set by hand, as a Makefile variable and as CI partitions validated against it, and resolve conflicts in it whenever two closures race. One adopter's hand list, compared on 2026-10-27 with what its corpus says, includes one spec still in progress and omits one complete spec that declares acceptance. This spec adds two filters that compose with `--status` and with `--ids-only`: `--implementation <state>`, over the frontmatter value, and `--has-acceptance`, true when `spec-spine verify <id>` would run at least one command, resolved the way `verify` resolves an amended block. The record gains `declaresAcceptance`, computed at compile, so the answer comes from the committed ledger like every other registry read.\n",
    "title": "The registry lists specs by implementation state and by whether verify would run anything"
  },
